<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Petro Kalnyshevsky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1690–1803</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Petro Kalnyshevsky was the last otaman of the Zaporozhian Sich, holding the office for most years from 1762 to 1775. When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine II</a>'s army destroyed the Sich in 1775 he was arrested and exiled to the Solovetsky Monastery in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-sea">White Sea</a>, where he was held for decades and died in 1803 at a great age. He is venerated as a saint in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p></div>
